# Every blob in this repository is stored with LF. Without this file, a Windows
# clone with core.autocrlf=true checks the working tree out as CRLF, and the
# repository's own tooling then fails on it: several build steps and tests match
# multi-line string literals against source files, and those needles are written
# with \n. tools/run-ai-eval-cloud-bounded.js is the clearest case — its patch
# guard reports "ditemukan 0" and the CI gate's own test set goes red locally
# while passing on the Linux runner.
#
# Pinning eol=lf keeps the working tree identical to the blobs on every platform,
# so a local run is a valid signal about CI.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be line-ending normalised.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.xlsx binary
*.gz binary
*.zip binary
